---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Cases from "../components/Cases.astro";
import { NotepadText } from "@lucide/astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Brand Designer"
  description="Portfolio of Grigorii Khralenok, brand and creative designer."
>
  <section id="hero" class="large">
    <div id="illustration">
      <img src="img/hero-illustration.svg" />
    </div>
    <div class="hero-text">
      <div id="title">
        <h1>
          <span id="h1-1">Looking for</span>
          <span id="h1-2">a graphic designer?</span>
        </h1>
      </div>
      <div id="subtitle">
        You found one. Hi, I’m Grigorii Khralenok. I design brand comunications
        and build systems and automations that make the work behind it run
        smoothly.
      </div>
      <div class="btns-wrapper center">
        <a class="btn" href="#cases">Explore cases</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="workflow">
    <div id="section-description">
      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>
        AI makes design faster, but not automatically better. Generated visuals
        drift off-brand, while manual production still takes time. My approach
        is simple: design first, systemize what works, automate what repeats.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div id="image">
      <img src="img/workflow-illustration.png" width="320" height="320" />
    </div>
    <div id="cards">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="number">1</div>
        <h3>Do the real design work</h3>
        <p>
          Every brand has its own logic. I learn it by working on real
          communication — audience, goals, constraints and team included.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="number">2</div>
        <h3>Turn it into a system</h3>
        <p>
          Once the visual language is clear, I turn it into practical rules and
          reusable patterns that keep everyday work fast and consistent.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="number">3</div>
        <h3>Automate the repetitive parts</h3>
        <p>
          When the system is stable, repetitive production becomes much easier
          to automate. I use TypeScript, Figma Plugin API, Codex and AI models
          to handle the mechanical work without giving up control.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="cases">
    <h2>Case studies</h2>
    <Cases />
  </section>
  <section id="knowhow">
    <div id="section-description">
      <h2>Know-how</h2>
      <p>
        I've constantly learn new things and collect them into notes. Here are
        my learnings that you can find interesting.
      </p>
      <div class="btns-wrapper">
        <a class="btn">Explore more</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <NotepadText />
        <a href="/">On-brand carousel mass production</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <NotepadText />
        <a href="/">Blog article infographics mass-production</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <NotepadText />
        <a href="/">Batch covers generation</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <NotepadText />
        <a href="/">Data-structures for automatization</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <NotepadText />
        <a href="/">Data-driven comparison graphic production</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <NotepadText />
        <a href="/">How to keep AI generation editable</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section id="faq">
    <div class="faq-container">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">Who is Grigorii?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            Grigorii is a brand designer with 10 years of experience creating
            visual identities, design systems, and marketing materials for B2B
            companies. His work covers websites, presentations, newsletters,
            campaigns, social media, events, and other key brand touchpoints.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">Why hire Grigorii?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            He combines strong hands-on design skills with system thinking.
            Beyond creating polished visual work, he builds templates,
            guidelines, and reusable components that help teams maintain quality
            and consistency as the volume of work grows.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question"
          >What is Grigorii’s strongest quality?</summary
        >
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            His strongest quality is the ability to turn complex ideas into
            clear visual systems. He looks beyond individual assets and
            considers how typography, layout, hierarchy, motion, and reusable
            design principles work together across the entire brand.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question"
          >What time zone does Grigorii work in?</summary
        >
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            Grigorii is based in Vietnam and works in the UTC+7 time zone. He
            can maintain regular overlap with teams in the UK and Europe and is
            comfortable adapting his schedule when projects require closer
            collaboration.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question"
          >What remote-work experience does Grigorii have?</summary
        >
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            Grigorii has several years of experience working independently with
            distributed teams, stakeholders, contractors, and clients across
            multiple countries. He is comfortable with asynchronous
            communication, documented workflows, structured handoffs, task
            tracking, and taking ownership of projects without constant
            supervision.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  section {
    font-family: var(--font-inter);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  section:not(.large),
  .hero-text > * {
    width: min(80ch, 100vw);
  }

  section:not(.large) {
    margin-block: 2rem 2rem;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-fredoka);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    --block-width: min(80ch, 100vw);
    color: inherit;
    line-height: 1;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 span:nth-child(1) {
    display: block;
    font-size: calc(var(--block-width) * 0.083);
    font-stretch: 103%;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  h1 span:nth-child(2) {
    display: block;
    font-size: calc(var(--block-width) * 0.0495);
    font-stretch: 105%;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  h2,
  h3 {
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
  }

  #hero {
    width: 100%;
    color: white;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .hero-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
    padding-block: 2rem 2rem;
  }

  #illustration {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 320/66;
    overflow: visible;
    z-index: 10;
  }

  #hero img {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
  }

  #title,
  #subtitle {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
  }

  #title {
    grid-column: span 2;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  #subtitle {
    margin-block: 3rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.07rem;
  }

  .btns-wrapper {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .btns-wrapper > * {
    flex-grow: 0;
  }

  .btns-wrapper.center{
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .btn {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 1rem 2rem;
    border-radius: 2rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    background: white;
    box-shadow: var(--color-neutral-100) 0 0.5rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--color-neutral-100);
  }

  #workflow {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    padding: 0 20vw;
    font-family: var(--font-inter);
  }

  #cards {
    grid-column: span 2;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  #section-description {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .number {
    top: -1rem;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    position: absolute;
    background: black;
    color: white;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border-radius: 999;
  }

  #image {
    display: flex;
    place-items: center;
  }

  #image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: unset;
  }

  .card {
    position: relative;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid black;
  }

  #knowhow {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    padding: 0 20vw;
  }

  #knowhow ul {
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  #section-description {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-items: center;
  }

  #knowhow li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid black;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .faq-container {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .faq-item {
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 1rem;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease-in-out;
    border: 1px solid black;
  }

  .faq-question {
    padding: var(--base-size);
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .faq-question::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-question::after {
    content: "+";
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .faq-item[open] .faq-question {
    color: var(--color-neutral-40);
    border-bottom: var(--dark-bg-border);
  }

  .faq-item[open] .faq-question::after {
    content: "−";
  }

  .faq-answer {
    padding: var(--base-size);
    font-size: calc(var(--base-size) * 0.8);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
